* Fender "Deluxe" model 5E3: cathodyne phase inverter (V2b, 12AX7), two 6V6GT in push-pull on a shared 250 ohm /
* 25u cathode bias with the screens on their own supply node and no negative feedback, the output transformer, and
* the 5Y3GT supply. B+1 (node a) is the rectifier / reservoir (16u), integrated by the engine; 5000 ohm + 16u make
* B+2 (screens), 22k + 16u make B+3 (node x: phase inverter and preamp).
*
* Assumptions where the drawing is silent or ambiguous (change them here, not in code):
*  - output transformer: 8k plate-to-plate onto the 8 ohm speaker (the 5E3 is usually quoted at 8k), 10 H per
*    primary half, 75 ohm per half, coupling like the other amps;
*  - the 220k grid leaks go to ground and the 1500 grid stoppers sit at the grids;
*  - the supply (355-0-355 transformer, 5Y3GT, no standby): a Thevenin rectifier source chosen for B+1 near 350 V
*    at idle, with the sag of this high-impedance rectifier; the cathode then sits near 19 V (about 38 mA per tube);
*  - RPREAMP stands for what V1 and V2a draw from B+3 (about 3 mA).

.nodes pin gp cj kc pp g1x g2x g1 g2 kcat a bb x pt pbm npt npb t8

S VAUDIO pin 65k 0
S VHT a 15 350

* Cathodyne: grid on the preamp output through 0.1u with a 1M leak to the cathode junction (1k5 / 56k divider),
* plate load 56k, outputs from the plate (V3) and the cathode (V4).
C C2 pin gp 0.1u
R R1M gp cj 1M
T V2B gp pp kc 12AX7
R R_PP x pp 56k
R RK2B kc cj 1k5
R RK2C cj 0 56k
C C3 pp g1x 0.1u
C C4 kc g2x 0.1u
R R220A g1x 0 220k
R R220B g2x 0 220k
R R1500A g1x g1 1500
R R1500B g2x g2 1500

* 6V6GT pair: screens on B+2 (node bb), shared cathode 250 ohm || 25u.
P V3 g1 pt bb kcat 6V6GT 1
P V4 g2 pbm bb kcat 6V6GT 1
R R250 kcat 0 250
C C25 kcat 0 25u

* Output transformer: primary halves around the B+1 centre tap, one 8 ohm secondary.
R DCR_PT pt npt 75
R DCR_PB pbm npb 75
.param n8 = 2*1/sqrt(8000/8)
* Core saturation: SAT is the flux (volt-seconds) where the extra magnetising current equals the linear one; ~full-power
* plate-to-plate swing / (2 pi f), with f about 28-30 Hz for the large Marshall / Soldano / Peavey / Fender cores, 50 to 65 Hz for the small AC30 / tweed cores.
.xfmr OT L=10 SAT=1.35
  W npt a 1 pri
  W a npb 1 pri
  W t8 0 n8 sec
  K pri pri 0.9998
  K pri sec 0.9993
.end
R RLOAD t8 0 8

* Supply: B+2 and B+3.
R R5000 a bb 5000
C C16B bb 0 16u
R R22K bb x 22k
C C16C x 0 16u
R RPREAMP x 0 75k
